<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean stock body says approves First Mutual IPO.</title>
<headline>S.Korean stock body says approves First Mutual IPO.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board has approved First Mutual Savings and Finance Co Ltd's application for an initial public offering (IPO), an SSB statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>First Mutual will offer 1.76 million shares at 6,300 won per share. Dongsuh Securities will underwrite the offering.</p>
<p>The offering will be held in mid-December and the shares will begin publicly trading in mid-January, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
